 [:db/cas 17592186176448 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The function has maximum values at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + nπ$.\n2. The function is zero at $x = \\frac{3π}{2}$.\n3. The range of the function is $[- π, π]$." "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function has maximum values at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + nπ$.\n- **II.** The function is zero at $x = \\frac{3π}{2}$.\n- **III.** The range of the function is $[- π, π]$."]
 {:db/id 17592186176448 :question/answer-fields ["field-q-27015/authored-checkbox-v1/I" "field-q-27015/authored-checkbox-v1/II" "field-q-27015/authored-checkbox-v1/III"] :db/ensure :question/validate}
 [:db/cas 17592186176449 :question/worked-solution nil "Cosine has zeros at x=pi/2+n*pi. At x=3pi/2+2n*pi it is zero, not maximal, and its range is [-1,1]. Only I is true."]
